WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.732 --> 00:00:16.054
When Pollyanna awoke the next morning, it was a beautiful day.

2
00:00:18.415 --> 00:00:21.856
Through an open window, she spotted Aunt Polly and Tom in the garden.

3
00:00:24.678 --> 00:00:27.639
Pollyanna ran outside and threw her arms around her aunt.

4
00:00:27.659 --> 00:00:29.219
"Aunt Polly!

5
00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:29.940
Aunt Polly!

6
00:00:30.464 --> 00:00:33.126
Today I'm glad just to be alive!"

7
00:00:33.146 --> 00:00:36.790
"Is this how you usually say good morning?"

8
00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:40.653
Aunt Polly scolded, releasing herself from Pollyanna's grip.

9
00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:43.976
"Only to people I love!"

10
00:00:43.996 --> 00:00:50.301
Pollyanna danced around Aunt Polly, who tried to frown but failed.

11
00:00:50.321 --> 00:00:55.306
"You may finish trimming those roses," Aunt Polly said to Tom.

12
00:00:56.487 --> 00:00:57.708
Then she hurried into the house.

13
00:00:59.912 --> 00:01:04.636
"You're so like your mother, little miss," said Tom, picking up his clippers.

14
00:01:04.656 --> 00:01:07.639
"I knew her when she was your age."

15
00:01:10.061 --> 00:01:11.142
Pollyanna gasped.

16
00:01:11.162 --> 00:01:12.443
"You did?

17
00:01:12.923 --> 00:01:14.965
Oh, please, tell me all about her!"

18
00:01:16.486 --> 00:01:19.589
Tom had barely begun to speak when a bell sounded from the house.

19
00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:23.212
The next minute Nancy flew out the back door.

20
00:01:23.232 --> 00:01:25.253
"Hurry up!"

21
00:01:26.094 --> 00:01:27.876
Nancy pulled Pollyanna toward the house.

22
00:01:28.864 --> 00:01:30.525
"That bell means it's time to eat.

23
00:01:31.385 --> 00:01:35.546
If you don't come quickly, it'll be hard to find anything to be glad about."

24
00:01:37.987 --> 00:01:41.448
At the breakfast table, Aunt Polly and Pollyanna ate in silence.

25
00:01:43.468 --> 00:01:46.989
As Nancy brought in more muffins, Aunt Polly noticed two flies.

26
00:01:47.009 --> 00:01:50.810
"Nancy, where did those flies come from?"

27
00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:53.131
"I don't know, ma'am."

28
00:01:53.151 --> 00:01:57.472
"They're probably my flies," Pollyanna said cheerfully.

29
00:01:58.496 --> 00:02:01.957
"A whole bunch of them were having a wonderful time in my room this morning."

30
00:02:05.138 --> 00:02:08.439
Struggling not to laugh, Nancy left the room with the muffins.

31
00:02:08.459 --> 00:02:11.840
"Nancy!" Aunt Polly called.

32
00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:16.321
Nancy returned with a serious look on her face and the muffins.

33
00:02:16.341 --> 00:02:23.423
"You may put down the muffins and close the windows in Miss Pollyanna's room," Aunt Polly said.

34
00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:27.564
"Pollyanna, keep those windows closed until we have screens.

35
00:02:28.576 --> 00:02:30.817
Flies spread all kinds of diseases."

36
00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:38.502
After breakfast Aunt Polly handed Pollyanna a pamphlet on flies.

37
00:02:40.063 --> 00:02:44.406
Pollyanna's eyes lit up when she saw an enlarged illustration of a fly's head.

38
00:02:44.426 --> 00:02:46.247
"Thank you!"

39
00:02:46.647 --> 00:02:48.408
she exclaimed, skipping from the room.

40
00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:54.432
Awhile later Aunt Polly went up to Pollyanna's room.

41
00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:02.183
"Oh, Aunt Polly, I never read anything so interesting in my life!"

42
00:03:02.684 --> 00:03:04.925
Pollyanna said with great enthusiasm.

43
00:03:04.945 --> 00:03:07.687
"I'm so glad you gave me that article.

44
00:03:08.428 --> 00:03:15.512
I had no idea flies—" "That's enough," said Aunt Polly, who'd meant the pamphlet as punishment for opening

45
00:03:15.552 --> 00:03:16.073
the windows.

46
00:03:16.093 --> 00:03:20.916
"I'd like to examine your clothes to see if they're suitable for living here with me."

47
00:03:23.678 --> 00:03:26.160
With great reluctance, Pollyanna opened her closet.

48
00:03:27.116 --> 00:03:28.857
"I'm afraid you'll think they're awful.

49
00:03:33.039 --> 00:03:36.120
You see, they all came from the donation box at church.

50
00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:41.102
Did you ever get your clothes from a donation box?"

51
00:03:41.142 --> 00:03:45.004
Seeing Aunt Polly's shocked face, Pollyanna quickly corrected herself.

52
00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:46.665
"Of course not.

53
00:03:47.025 --> 00:03:51.006
You're rich—though in this room it's easy for me to forget you're rich.

54
00:03:51.827 --> 00:03:57.174
It was hard to play the game with my clothes, but Fath—" Pollyanna stopped when she remembered Aunt

55
00:03:57.234 --> 00:03:59.235
Polly didn't want to hear about her father.

56
00:04:00.276 --> 00:04:03.518
Aunt Polly abruptly started examining Pollyanna's clothes.

57
00:04:03.538 --> 00:04:08.161
"I assume you went to school?"

58
00:04:08.181 --> 00:04:13.464
"Yes, and sometimes Fath—I mean, I was taught at home too."

59
00:04:14.845 --> 00:04:16.046
Aunt Polly looked stern.

60
00:04:16.066 --> 00:04:21.249
"You'll start school in the fall, but in the meantime, you'll be on a strict schedule.

61
00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:24.672
Every day before breakfast, you'll tidy this room.

62
00:04:25.756 --> 00:04:28.577
At nine o'clock you'll read aloud to me for half an hour.

63
00:04:29.757 --> 00:04:34.758
On Wednesdays and Saturdays, you'll spend the rest of the morning in the kitchen with Nancy, learning to

64
00:04:34.798 --> 00:04:37.999
cook. On the other mornings, I'll teach you to sew.

65
00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:41.280
You'll spend your afternoons practicing the piano."

66
00:04:42.601 --> 00:04:43.761
Pollyanna squirmed.

67
00:04:43.781 --> 00:04:47.422
"I don't really like playing the piano."

68
00:04:47.442 --> 00:04:53.103
"I'm sure that's true, but you will take piano lessons here."

69
00:04:56.096 --> 00:04:57.517
Pollyanna sighed deeply.

70
00:04:57.537 --> 00:05:02.139
"With all these activities, you haven't left me time to just live.

71
00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:07.562
You know, to climb hills and talk to Tom and explore the town."

72
00:05:09.123 --> 00:05:11.204
Now it was Aunt Polly's turn to sigh.

73
00:05:11.224 --> 00:05:18.028
"I'm doing my duty by ensuring that you have proper care and instruction.

74
00:05:18.808 --> 00:05:20.930
You must do your duty too.

75
00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:24.912
Don't waste these opportunities and don't be ungrateful.

76
00:05:26.036 --> 00:05:28.157
There will be some time for play."

77
00:05:30.198 --> 00:05:33.439
Aunt Polly was halfway down the stairs when Pollyanna called after her.

78
00:05:33.459 --> 00:05:35.720
"What did you think of my clothes?"

79
00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:38.582
"We'll go shopping this afternoon.

80
00:05:39.462 --> 00:05:43.624
If I let you appear in public in those clothes, I wouldn't be doing my duty!"
